  "hatarakiHelpTitle": "{page, select, work{your Tamas at work} level{total level} likes{what they're good at} stuff{materials} trip{expeditions} map{the map} orders{orders} town{the town} market{the market} homes{rooms} visit{visiting} coins{coins and prizes} other{?}}",
  "hatarakiHelpBody": "{page, select, work{In «skills», pick a task and the Tama who will do it. They keep working even with the app closed, for up to 12 hours. Every finished task gives experience to its skill, and sometimes something extra.} level{Each skill goes from level 0 to 99. Your total level is the sum of all your skill levels. It opens more slots so more Tamas can work at once: at 40, 100, 200, 350, 550, 800 and 1100.} likes{Each Tama has a knack depending on their personality: they work 15 % faster at these skills. A good mood makes them faster too: pet them or feed them. You'll also see this when creating a Tama.} stuff{Woodcutting, fishing, mining, farming and foraging gather materials. Cooking, carpentry, smithing, tailoring, tea, jewelcrafting, pottery, dyeing, building, writing, brewing and magic turn them into other things, and study reads books just for the experience. Tamas who fish, farm or mine can use bait, fertiliser or fuses. If something runs out, the Tama waits and goes back to work as soon as there's more. In the storehouse, everything says where it comes from and what it's for.} trip{Send 1 to 3 free Tamas with food. Strength (expedition level, knack, gear from the storehouse and the rune) against the place's difficulty gives the success. They bring things you can't get any other way, and sometimes a treasure: a gachaken ticket. The farther, the likelier (from 0.2 % in the meadow to 5 % on the moon, times the success), and they're claimed on their own, one per hour.} map{Every place has a map each day, the same for everyone. Choose the route by tapping one spot per column: loot, rare finds, dangers (they need strength or a healing potion), rests (no food) and chests (more treasure). A map, a sight potion or a guide clears the fog. With ginmon you can pay a porter (more loot) and a cart (less time). If you call them back early, they bring what they found in the spots already passed.} orders{Every day the town's notice board has 3 orders (up to 5 if you upgrade it) and a big order. They ask for things you already know how to make and pay more ginmon than selling them, sometimes with experience or something rare. The big order asks for more, sometimes a parcel from the errand spot on a map, and pays a gachaken ticket: one a day. Once a day you can swap an order for another one, for a fee. What you earn counts for the wealth leaderboard.} town{With ginmon and building parts you put up and upgrade the buildings, from level 1 to 5. The workshop, kiln, dock, greenhouse and tower speed up skills; the library and tower open books, maps and runes, and the inn helps with trips and holds your Tamas' rooms. Every level shows on the map: flower pots, a lantern, a tree and, at 5, its banner. The shop sells a few things every day, at 4 times what they sell for. Spending ginmon doesn't lower you on the leaderboard: what counts is what you earn.} market{Every day, the same for everyone and even without a market, 6 things sell for more (some single items and everything from a couple of skills) and everything from 2 other skills sells for less. The market tells you which: always what goes down and, of what goes up, more the higher its level. At level 3 it also shows tomorrow's, so you can keep what's about to go up.} homes{Each Tama can have a room at the inn, 6×6 squares (you can go in even before the inn is built). The first one is cheap (ginmon and a couple of beams) and the next ones cost more. Furniture is made in carpentry, pottery, dyeing, tailoring, writing and magic (most pieces need a plan, bought at the shop or given by orders), and a few are only sold at the shop. Place, move and turn them as you like. Comfort comes from how much furniture there is, whether it matches (same style: rustic, marine, elegant, magic or floral) and whether the Tama likes the style: calm ones love floral; playful, marine; shy, elegant; cheeky, rustic; and sleepy, magic. With a room, the Tama rests and works here in at least 25 % spirits, up to 80 % in the comfiest room. Their spirits in Ibasho don't change.} visit{With the friends button on the map, or from a friend's profile, you can visit their town: their buildings, their Tamas, what they're doing, their rooms, their best skills and their wealth. It's look-only: nothing can be touched. You see it as they left it the last time they played.} coins{Every minute with the channel open gives 1 coin, up to 20 a day. The ginmon you earn by selling counts for the daily and weekly leaderboards, and everything you've ever earned, for the «all-time» table.} other{?}}",
